On Wednesday 29 September 2010 05:22:17 Stela Selckiku wrote:
> How long should a word be marked with "za'e"?  Does it mean that a
> word is being used for the very first time, or should it be used as
> long as a word is likely to be unfamiliar or isn't yet found in
> dictionaries?
>
> I'm thinking particularly of a situation that I often find myself in:
> I want to use a word that I already thought of a long time ago, but I
> only used it a few times before, and no one has particularly noticed
> it, or at least no one uses it except me.  Should I mark those words
> with "za'e" when I bring them out again?

I don't use it often if at all, but I think it warrants use if a word is us=
ed=20
in a different sense than the normal meaning (common in mathematics,=20
where "ring" and "group" have meanings completely different from the normal=
),=20
or if it's a lujvo whose meaning is unlikely to be figured out.

Btw, I don't think that the usual words "djine" and "girzu" and "foldi" sho=
uld=20
be used for the mathematical meanings. They are types of girzu (the ring,=
=20
IIRR, is dilcygri), but just plain "girzu" is not right. "Continuous",=20
though, is close enough to the normal meaning.

